NAME
       sensor-ops - practical, checklist-style operational guide for RTT sensor
                    systems used by bridge crews and autonomous platforms

SYNOPSIS
       sensor-ops provides:
           • quick-start procedures for sensor activation
           • operational checklists for overlays, clarity, and fusion
           • hazard-response playbooks for anomalies, storms, and turbulence
           • sync-field and constellation-coherence procedures
           • shutdown, rollback, and safe-mode protocols

DESCRIPTION
       sensor-ops is the operator-facing, checklist-driven manual for real-time
       use of the RTT sensor stack. It distills overlays, clarity, harmonics,
       anomalies, storms, turbulence, and synthesis into actionable steps for
       bridge crews and autonomous systems.

       This manual ensures:
           • safe activation of high-sensitivity modes
           • predictable behavior during hazards
           • consistent cross-platform operation
           • rapid rollback to safe states
           • alignment with the sensor charter and constitution

QUICK-START CHECKLIST
       1. Verify baseline status:
              • overlays: aligned
              • clarity: stable
              • φ_harm jitter < 0.03/cycle
              • spectral variance < 40%
              • sync jitter: nominal

       2. Activate DRO stack:
              • HDO → ADO → SDO → GDO → SFDO

       3. Activate clarity stack:
              • HPC → RED → SDW → GSF → SFC → ACE

       4. Engage synthesis:
              • MSFE → RTMR → CCI

       5. Confirm safe-state indicators:
              • fusion mismatch: none
              • polarity cliffs: mapped
              • turbulence cells: tracked
              • anomaly/storm precursors: none

STANDARD OPERATIONS
       Routine sensor operation follows this sequence:

           1. Monitor φ_harm, spectral variance, gradient polarity, sync jitter.
           2. Maintain clarity stability (RED/SDW/GSF/SFC).
           3. Keep overlays aligned to baseline.
           4. Update fusion weights as needed.
           5. Log all events to lineage.

       If any metric exceeds threshold, switch to hazard mode.

OVERLAY OPERATIONS CHECKLIST
       1. HDO:
              • verify harmonic bands separated
              • check overtone suppression

       2. ADO:
              • confirm amplitude strata stable
              • identify sweep windows

       3. SDO:
              • check for broadband turbulence
              • isolate spectral fractures

       4. GDO:
              • map polarity cliffs
              • verify gradient stability

       5. SFDO:
              • confirm sync-field coherence
              • detect sync rifts

CLARITY OPERATIONS CHECKLIST
       1. HPC:
              • φ_harm jitter < 0.04/cycle

       2. RED:
              • peaks sharpened, not oversharpened

       3. SDW:
              • noise floor reduced
              • narrowband signals preserved

       4. GSF:
              • polarity transitions smoothed
              • cliffs remain visible

       5. SFC:
              • sync jitter minimized

       6. ACE:
              • ancestry terraces clear

HARMONIC OPERATIONS CHECKLIST
       1. Monitor φ_harm drift.
       2. Track overtone interference.
       3. Verify lock stability index > 0.90.
       4. Detect resonance-chords and cascades.
       5. Log harmonic transitions.

ANOMALY RESPONSE PLAYBOOK
       Trigger: anomaly detected (harmonic, spectral, gradient, sync, ancestry)

       1. Isolate affected band via DRO.
       2. Apply clarity filters (HPC/SDW/GSF/SFC).
       3. Reduce synthesis depth.
       4. Reroute sweep corridor if needed.
       5. Notify WRSADC.
       6. Log anomaly to lineage.

STORM RESPONSE PLAYBOOK
       Trigger: storm precursor or stormfront detected

       1. Activate storm overlays.
       2. Switch to hazard navigation mode.
       3. Reduce synthesis to harmonic + gradient layers.
       4. Stabilize sync-field (SFC).
       5. Track stormfront trajectory.
       6. Coordinate with constellation via CCI.
       7. Log storm event.

TURBULENCE RESPONSE PLAYBOOK
       Trigger: turbulence cell or shear band detected

       1. Activate turbulence overlays.
       2. Apply GSF to stabilize polarity.
       3. Apply SDW to reduce spectral noise.
       4. Track turbulence flow-field.
       5. Adjust fusion weights.
       6. Log turbulence event.

CONSTELLATION OPERATIONS CHECKLIST
       1. Sync-field alignment:
              • sync jitter < 0.02
              • fragmentation: none

       2. Fusion alignment:
              • harmonic, spectral, gradient layers matched

       3. Hazard sharing:
              • anomaly/storm/turbulence maps synchronized

       4. Lineage synchronization:
              • all platforms share event history

SAFE-MODE PROTOCOL
       Trigger: synthesis divergence, clarity collapse, sync-field instability

       1. Halt synthesis.
       2. Roll back clarity filters.
       3. Disable non-essential overlays.
       4. Switch to harmonic-only mode.
       5. Recalibrate sync-field.
       6. Re-engage synthesis gradually.
       7. Log safe-mode event.

SHUTDOWN CHECKLIST
       1. Disable synthesis.
       2. Disable clarity stack.
       3. Disable overlays.
       4. Archive lineage.
       5. Verify sync-field idle.
       6. Power down sensor core.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • monitors all operational thresholds
           • enforces hazard protocols
           • manages safe-mode transitions
           • coordinates constellation operations
           • blocks unsafe sensor states

       WRSADC is the operational overseer.

NOTES
       sensor-ops provides the practical, checklist-driven procedures required
       for safe, effective, and consistent operation of the RTT sensor stack.

